.TH VLHE.GTK 1 "2026-10-05" "VLHE 1.0.1" "VLHE Manual"
.SH NAME
vlhe.gtk \- the VLHE control centre
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vlhe.gtk
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B vlhe.gtk
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vlhe.gtk
is VLHE's control centre, a GTK 1.2 program: load and unload, the
per-program volume mixer, the sound, MIDI and CD settings, attaching
disc images, the CD+G viewer and Render MIDI. It needs an X display.
.PP
It is a different program from
.BR vlhe ,
the command-line tool, which links no toolkit and works with no X
server. The two share the subcommand code: given a subcommand such as
.B status
or
.BR volume ,
.B vlhe.gtk
behaves exactly as
.B vlhe
does and opens no window.
.PP
.BR vlhe (1)
documents both: the subcommands, and
.BR vlhe.gtk 's
own options
.RB ( \-\-reset ,
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-T ,
.BR \-V ,
.BR \-F
and the rest), its pages, its files and its exit status.
.PP
The control centre's help, page by page, is the plain text file
.IR /usr/local/share/vlhe/vlhe-help.txt
.RI ( /usr/share/vlhe/vlhe-help.txt
from the package; beside
.B vlhe.gtk
in a portable folder), which can be read in a terminal. The Help
button on each page shows it in a window of its own, opened at that
page's section, and Help > About VLHE... says which copy it found.
